{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1578643298,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1NDc5MjU2NDQ=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/4005","origin":"github"},"title":"get() should rename 'origin' of a subdataset to match superds remote is was cloned from","message":"Aspect of original #1956 reported by @mvdoc on behalf of @yoh\n\nIf a subdataset is found to be available as a subdataset underneath a superdataset's clone/remote, and ends up being installed from that location, its origin remote should match the one of the superdataset's remote.\n\nImplementing such a behavior will counteract the fix for https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3926 in #3966","files":null}]}